WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.328 --> 00:00:06.310
"Wake up, Demi!"

2
00:00:13.974 --> 00:00:15.095
Jo said softly.

3
00:00:15.115 --> 00:00:18.137
"I need you to get up right now."

4
00:00:18.157 --> 00:00:27.361
"I just went to bed," Demi said in a sleepy voice, "so it can't be morning yet."

5
00:00:27.381 --> 00:00:36.122
"You're right, but your father is ill, and we must go to him," Jo said, beginning to sob.

6
00:00:36.142 --> 00:00:38.483
"My poor John!"

7
00:00:40.444 --> 00:00:44.126
Suddenly Demi was aware that something was terribly wrong.

8
00:00:45.427 --> 00:00:48.769
No one ever called him John—a name he shared with his father.

9
00:00:48.789 --> 00:00:52.031
"Is Papa very sick?"

10
00:00:52.531 --> 00:00:53.111
he asked.

11
00:00:54.572 --> 00:00:58.694
Jo swallowed hard and said, "We're going to say good-bye to him.

12
00:01:00.475 --> 00:01:02.809
Get dressed quickly, and come to my study.

13
00:01:03.169 --> 00:01:04.230
I must wake Daisy."

14
00:01:08.052 --> 00:01:11.995
As he dressed, Demi sensed that his world was about to change.

15
00:01:13.396 --> 00:01:18.179
Daisy was soon ready, and the twins got into the carriage with Jo and the professor.

16
00:01:20.261 --> 00:01:23.863
All the way into town, Daisy and Demi held hands.

17
00:01:26.345 --> 00:01:30.588
The next morning breakfast was a dismal meal without Jo at the table.

18
00:01:33.140 --> 00:01:36.481
When it was time for school, the professor's chair was empty too.

19
00:01:36.501 --> 00:01:39.882
"What are we supposed to do today?"

20
00:01:40.342 --> 00:01:41.802
Jack asked in confusion.

21
00:01:41.822 --> 00:01:47.024
"I don't feel like playing," Tommy said, and the others agreed.

22
00:01:47.044 --> 00:01:51.785
"Let's try to do our lessons as usual," Dan suggested.

23
00:01:51.805 --> 00:01:55.186
"That'll make the day go faster and please the professor."

24
00:01:55.206 --> 00:01:58.047
"But who will be the teacher?"

25
00:01:58.587 --> 00:01:59.307
Nan asked.

26
00:01:59.327 --> 00:02:07.722
"I'll teach you about wolves and foxes," Dan said, "and then maybe you could read quietly while I

27
00:02:07.742 --> 00:02:09.162
take Teddy outside to play."

28
00:02:10.622 --> 00:02:15.084
And that's what the children were doing when the professor returned home later in the morning.

29
00:02:16.424 --> 00:02:21.025
The children knew at once from his expression that John Brookes had died.

30
00:02:21.045 --> 00:02:23.526
"Don't cry, Papa!"

31
00:02:24.006 --> 00:02:26.087
Rob said, running to his father.

32
00:02:26.107 --> 00:02:28.828
"We've been doing our lessons!"

33
00:02:29.288 --> 00:02:29.948
Tommy said.

34
00:02:31.048 --> 00:02:32.109
"Thank you, everyone."

35
00:02:32.449 --> 00:02:34.870
Mr. Bauer scooped Rob into his arms.

36
00:02:34.890 --> 00:02:38.451
"You've made a hard day easier.

37
00:02:39.632 --> 00:02:42.853
Unfortunately, I must return to town soon."

38
00:02:42.873 --> 00:02:47.255
"When will Mama come home?"

39
00:02:47.595 --> 00:02:48.315
Rob asked.

40
00:02:48.335 --> 00:02:52.397
"Tonight," the professor said, kissing his son.

41
00:02:52.417 --> 00:02:56.239
"Right now Aunt Meg needs her."

42
00:02:56.259 --> 00:03:02.013
"Teddy's been crying for her, and he slapped Asia and was terribly naughty!"

43
00:03:02.433 --> 00:03:06.495
Rob reported, hoping that news would bring his mother home immediately.

44
00:03:07.876 --> 00:03:09.016
But it did not.

45
00:03:11.617 --> 00:03:16.899
Professor Bauer left again, and for the rest of the day, the house was very still, like a

46
00:03:16.979 --> 00:03:24.202
Sunday. Nan and the boys spent their time walking, sitting in the willow tree, and tending to their

47
00:03:24.222 --> 00:03:32.899
pets. At dusk Jo and the professor returned home, but Demi and Daisy had stayed in town with

48
00:03:32.939 --> 00:03:33.399
their mother.

49
00:03:35.220 --> 00:03:36.220
"Where's my baby?"

50
00:03:36.821 --> 00:03:39.582
an exhausted Jo said upon entering the house.

51
00:03:39.602 --> 00:03:42.704
"Here!" Teddy cried.

52
00:03:42.724 --> 00:03:47.887
"My Danny took care of me all day, and I was good!"

53
00:03:49.327 --> 00:03:55.291
Jo turned to thank Dan, but he was whispering to the others, "Don't bother her right now."

54
00:03:55.311 --> 00:04:01.274
"No, children, please don't stay away from me," Jo said with a tired smile.

55
00:04:01.294 --> 00:04:07.736
"I've neglected you all day, so I'll rest with Teddy in my study, while you bring me my

56
00:04:07.796 --> 00:04:08.717
supper on a tray."

57
00:04:10.497 --> 00:04:16.520
There was a general stampede into the dining room, where everyone fought for the honor of bringing Jo

58
00:04:16.580 --> 00:04:17.160
some food.

59
00:04:17.180 --> 00:04:21.382
"Calm yourselves!"

60
00:04:21.742 --> 00:04:22.702
the professor said.

61
00:04:22.722 --> 00:04:28.521
"Half of you can bring her supper, while the rest can clear the dishes away."

62
00:04:30.281 --> 00:04:36.203
Another mother might have found it annoying to have children upsetting cups and rattling spoons while they tried

63
00:04:36.243 --> 00:04:36.963
to be quiet.

64
00:04:38.363 --> 00:04:44.025
But that night Jo felt especially fond of the children, touched by their concern for her.

65
00:04:45.365 --> 00:04:50.986
Several of them lacked mothers or fathers or both, which made their efforts even more endearing.

66
00:04:52.327 --> 00:04:56.468
When Jo's tray had been removed, Dan offered to put Teddy to bed.

67
00:04:59.156 --> 00:05:04.040
"I wish I could do something helpful," Nat said with a sigh.

68
00:05:04.060 --> 00:05:07.283
"You can, dear," said Jo.

69
00:05:07.303 --> 00:05:13.448
"Get your violin and play some of the sweet songs that Uncle Laurie sent last week."

70
00:05:16.750 --> 00:05:22.035
As Jo listened, she fell asleep in her chair and forgot her sorrow for an hour.

71
00:05:24.056 --> 00:05:28.360
A few days later, the children went into town for John Brookes' funeral.

72
00:05:29.660 --> 00:05:31.322
Everyone was there—Mr.

73
00:05:31.362 --> 00:05:31.742
and Mrs.

74
00:05:31.802 --> 00:05:35.005
March, Uncle Laurie and Aunt Amy, old Mr.

75
00:05:35.045 --> 00:05:36.606
Laurence, and a few friends.

76
00:05:38.788 --> 00:05:44.172
Mr. March conducted the simple service at Meg's house, and the boys did their part by singing a

77
00:05:44.212 --> 00:05:53.120
hymn. That evening at Plumfield, everyone sat in the schoolroom, talking of John Brookes.

78
00:05:53.140 --> 00:05:56.703
"He wasn't a rich man, was he?"

79
00:05:57.123 --> 00:05:57.884
Jack asked.

80
00:05:58.948 --> 00:06:00.529
"No," Tommy said.

81
00:06:02.030 --> 00:06:04.311
Jack was disappointed in Tommy's answer.

82
00:06:04.331 --> 00:06:10.075
"And he never did anything to boast about—he was just a good man?"

83
00:06:10.095 --> 00:06:13.857
"That's right," the professor said.

84
00:06:13.877 --> 00:06:20.341
"He was just a good, honest man who loved his family and took care of everyone.

85
00:06:21.541 --> 00:06:25.884
He lived the best life of all, better than any rich or famous man."

86
00:06:28.692 --> 00:06:35.677
When the twins returned to school, Demi seemed more serious and tackled his math assignments with gusto.

87
00:06:36.958 --> 00:06:40.661
This puzzled the professor because Demi had always hated math.

88
00:06:40.681 --> 00:06:46.985
"I'm going to be a bookkeeper like my father," Demi explained one day.

89
00:06:48.666 --> 00:06:54.451
Another day he said to Jo, "Papa told me to take care of my mother and the girls—what

90
00:06:54.491 --> 00:06:56.032
can I do to earn some money?"

91
00:06:57.868 --> 00:07:02.911
"He didn't mean now," Jo said, ruffling her nephew's hair affectionately.

92
00:07:03.711 --> 00:07:09.615
But Demi looked so disappointed that she quickly added, "I'm sure we could pay you to rake leaves."

93
00:07:11.716 --> 00:07:14.617
As time passed, Jo gave him more jobs.

94
00:07:16.698 --> 00:07:21.901
Demi was happy when he could provide a dollar each for his mother, Daisy, and baby Josy.

95
00:07:23.282 --> 00:07:28.906
He often said the words "my father" with gentle pride and announced that he wanted to be called

96
00:07:29.027 --> 00:07:30.451
John when he was older.
